[{:db/id "q-352528/field-1/5f07a936a58ad5b1fe64f09dbf81dd600c860a1cc3c2bef4576d6bcf9c392515" :answer/id #uuid "92bb398e-b81d-5300-b8d4-4689b34a5b1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20t^3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352528/field-1/d93b909386fdff5687f6bc92cbdcc71b5bfc1473c1ae970e5d0bb8f74303045e" :answer/id #uuid "0cb30bd5-72c8-58ec-a33b-05ce8fd86d71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5t^3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352528/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "72a75de3-3688-5274-bfa9-7835e374b9a4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352528/field-1/5f07a936a58ad5b1fe64f09dbf81dd600c860a1cc3c2bef4576d6bcf9c392515" :answer-field/choices ["q-352528/field-1/5f07a936a58ad5b1fe64f09dbf81dd600c860a1cc3c2bef4576d6bcf9c392515" "q-352528/field-1/d93b909386fdff5687f6bc92cbdcc71b5bfc1473c1ae970e5d0bb8f74303045e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352528/field-2/1e606ff2d24d02e55a12d42ec3bb5136169f9802b114b362eb2744f7a5e9d074" :answer/id #uuid "62350b20-ed7f-5dbe-8931-f99aed713db1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{t^3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352528/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb89c173-c41d-5630-b9c8-ca1f3d16d71b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352528/field-2/1e606ff2d24d02e55a12d42ec3bb5136169f9802b114b362eb2744f7a5e9d074" :answer-field/choices ["q-352528/field-2/1e606ff2d24d02e55a12d42ec3bb5136169f9802b114b362eb2744f7a5e9d074"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352528" :question/id #uuid "538913ea-705b-5c27-a825-df7179576972" :question/math-academy-id "q-352528" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨5{t}^{4}+3,\\,\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$\n\n$v=⟨${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{4}+3),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨20{t}^{3},-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-352528/field-1" "q-352528/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dccdc3ad-6acb-57ae-83ef-95ffedfbff2f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352528"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121714/selection/1e89844b9fe43cd16cef8eb5ad2af2b300574cb6a2b2cfb8d567f8867d511220" :answer/id #uuid "8d61de6e-3918-5859-a37e-70330c865b87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=⟨{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121714/selection/2fd2246176e86c18bc5b4aee62b3853f1cdbb4b9f1a3b11f4775df469235c77c" :answer/id #uuid "2202dd43-2a1d-55e5-9743-f42987f01d5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=⟨2t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121714/selection/fd1395e0e83c94ce765972403d0420fc382649ea9d2e11519efa396a45efb1a9" :answer/id #uuid "82f92e2f-99ea-58cf-b3bd-67ecc0f66b43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=⟨t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},-5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121714/selection/a0d147845eda5278f3460f0f6ef0e9f322f665f16ae70876953c53583e4011d4" :answer/id #uuid "3a268b8a-0219-5d61-9f8d-efad780e3f56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=⟨{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},-5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121714/selection/2741199b48db2107c7c2d497155b2ce849fa53d8d8e21528835f51bf8fe3e4d2" :answer/id #uuid "109c68ca-85dd-51de-b1ad-d472991df4ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=⟨2t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},-5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121714/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "684fc375-4774-502f-934b-323e3d4abff7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121714/selection/2741199b48db2107c7c2d497155b2ce849fa53d8d8e21528835f51bf8fe3e4d2" :answer-field/choices ["q-121714/selection/1e89844b9fe43cd16cef8eb5ad2af2b300574cb6a2b2cfb8d567f8867d511220" "q-121714/selection/2fd2246176e86c18bc5b4aee62b3853f1cdbb4b9f1a3b11f4775df469235c77c" "q-121714/selection/fd1395e0e83c94ce765972403d0420fc382649ea9d2e11519efa396a45efb1a9" "q-121714/selection/a0d147845eda5278f3460f0f6ef0e9f322f665f16ae70876953c53583e4011d4" "q-121714/selection/2741199b48db2107c7c2d497155b2ce849fa53d8d8e21528835f51bf8fe3e4d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121714" :question/id #uuid "ccee9cb0-6d5e-5df1-a880-6088579e51f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-121714" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},2-5t⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{{t}^{2}-1}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-5t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-121714/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dccdc3ad-6acb-57ae-83ef-95ffedfbff2f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121714"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121715/selection/3252cb473e228694fc5dbdbdd62745f7c89e362435724d32811c19fc2b69d621" :answer/id #uuid "7529f4ff-d3d8-5929-a071-d9cbee406159" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=⟨-6,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121715/selection/a02efb10daadfbff2f8d1e8a11e343636297f4b878147c1f5f6a0777e915b0c3" :answer/id #uuid "e8bfdea3-ca13-54b3-ba03-87035e821200" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=⟨-6t,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121715/selection/9fce5ad95bcaf6d2c61c202075e18f4f2b4781faf03edcab64eeec11d37cab36" :answer/id #uuid "c00c2874-a796-5831-9b68-202b9869a788" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=⟨-6t,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121715/selection/817dce9738eeaae17033ed6d13ccc880c53e8ba79f47603cdf13206709ff17b9" :answer/id #uuid "db87cb5f-599f-5284-8b72-909b5399c076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=⟨-6t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121715/selection/f2ba95f0953f194c7e86198fffcfb4ac9ca0ceff857a6c1f444518dc935b3c10" :answer/id #uuid "a6c045f2-3845-5d15-9a07-b5f55fe77645" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=⟨-6,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121715/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "98cb2c02-8a2a-5607-8a2e-1f968290202c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121715/selection/9fce5ad95bcaf6d2c61c202075e18f4f2b4781faf03edcab64eeec11d37cab36" :answer-field/choices ["q-121715/selection/3252cb473e228694fc5dbdbdd62745f7c89e362435724d32811c19fc2b69d621" "q-121715/selection/a02efb10daadfbff2f8d1e8a11e343636297f4b878147c1f5f6a0777e915b0c3" "q-121715/selection/9fce5ad95bcaf6d2c61c202075e18f4f2b4781faf03edcab64eeec11d37cab36" "q-121715/selection/817dce9738eeaae17033ed6d13ccc880c53e8ba79f47603cdf13206709ff17b9" "q-121715/selection/f2ba95f0953f194c7e86198fffcfb4ac9ca0ceff857a6c1f444518dc935b3c10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121715" :question/id #uuid "dff3dcdc-b2c7-599a-a4a3-788e4f4701f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-121715" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨1-3{t}^{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-3{t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6t,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-121715/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dccdc3ad-6acb-57ae-83ef-95ffedfbff2f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121715"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-31637"] :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{3/2}+4{t}^{2},\\,11t-1⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3/2}+4{t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(11t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t}+8t,\\,11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-352544/field-1/59bb402bb4f35edfccafee5b3c66e177eaca41fe20a69168b0f9c27e7c72c240" :answer/id #uuid "97330db3-9aa0-52b4-8597-c507766186d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\cos(2t)+5\\sin(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352544/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b73c94c-29b2-5688-96cc-1afae4ce8a28" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352544/field-1/59bb402bb4f35edfccafee5b3c66e177eaca41fe20a69168b0f9c27e7c72c240" :answer-field/choices ["q-352544/field-1/59bb402bb4f35edfccafee5b3c66e177eaca41fe20a69168b0f9c27e7c72c240"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352544" :question/id #uuid "2e5e831f-7898-5930-bb11-0aa076c84717" :question/math-academy-id "q-352544" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$\n\n$v=⟨${{field-1}}$\\,,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)⟩$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-352544/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dccdc3ad-6acb-57ae-83ef-95ffedfbff2f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352544"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352549/field-1/dab748088abc997714e4d3192f18fc2445f30ef4888eda35234cd97f2815c702" :answer/id #uuid "6bfde910-68b3-513a-9ca7-da72109081db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352549/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d5a8823-c9ea-586b-a4ca-5385e642140e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352549/field-1/dab748088abc997714e4d3192f18fc2445f30ef4888eda35234cd97f2815c702" :answer-field/choices ["q-352549/field-1/dab748088abc997714e4d3192f18fc2445f30ef4888eda35234cd97f2815c702"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352549/field-2/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128" :answer/id #uuid "53d05e1f-6400-5c09-9dc7-781d19a3ad30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352549/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2788e568-11ac-5055-babc-82c9a4d9b241" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352549/field-2/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128" :answer-field/choices ["q-352549/field-2/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352549" :question/id #uuid "4eacfe13-b746-5b0a-9f45-3716d82f5075" :question/math-academy-id "q-352549" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\frac{7}{t+1},\\,\\frac{5t}{{t}^{2}+1}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=2.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$v(2)=⟨${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{7}{t+1}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{5t}{{t}^{2}+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{7}{(t+1)^{2}},\\frac{5-5{t}^{2}}{({t}^{2}+1)^{2}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2,$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨-\\frac{7}{(2+1)^{2}},\\,\\frac{5-5(2)^{2}}{((2)^{2}+1)^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{7}{9},\\,-\\frac{3}{5}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-352549/field-1" "q-352549/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca363e2-c7b7-5196-bd38-10bcc30123ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352549"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347187/field-1/0086db6077a62a5e2d9c771f7cdf57bea92b1de496b4d9b1d9c50dc1e5b58991" :answer/id #uuid "00027b2b-350f-5111-bff3-1e7b0aae3e17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347187/field-1/c59421689e9802bbe55dc885ef3b88a565922fc724e5a7225b403918fe48989b" :answer/id #uuid "8c41913b-70ea-5986-b091-71e0c7e9bb61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347187/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d60a38b7-e341-5aae-8e5e-eb891f24c4d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347187/field-1/0086db6077a62a5e2d9c771f7cdf57bea92b1de496b4d9b1d9c50dc1e5b58991" :answer-field/choices ["q-347187/field-1/0086db6077a62a5e2d9c771f7cdf57bea92b1de496b4d9b1d9c50dc1e5b58991" "q-347187/field-1/c59421689e9802bbe55dc885ef3b88a565922fc724e5a7225b403918fe48989b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347187/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "046722ce-4100-5567-8ec0-d1b11e52926a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347187/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ebae0984-fc4c-5b31-bd1d-3109bba4b937" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347187/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-347187/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347187" :question/id #uuid "799e038f-f33f-55b4-83d1-4c2e6a2e311f" :question/math-academy-id "q-347187" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨7{t}^{2},\\,-18⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=5.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$v(5)=⟨${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7{t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-18)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨14t,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=5,$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(5) & =⟨14(5),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨70,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-347187/field-1" "q-347187/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca363e2-c7b7-5196-bd38-10bcc30123ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347187"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-51321/selection/0bf0647c0d1d4cbdf6d8778630c4c8d1a77f0c9076f89ec0ac34fbdb2aeb5145" :answer/id #uuid "40be7ceb-78f5-5ef7-a260-6bf715eaedd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨0,\\,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51321/selection/46959d84f4ab7edcbf6a72c5825078c3adf82b1a24e5ebe6f94127028ac0c909" :answer/id #uuid "1597c9dc-17cc-5b41-bdee-c2722dd4ad2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51321/selection/a1d6a6791698f26fa6ae881b564c930292d4d77c0a2dd67b51115a82631a6409" :answer/id #uuid "36ce3d41-5ce1-5eec-84ee-e4db192d93c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨1,\\,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51321/selection/2a23ad8446f30a46eec178d617017260911d066e90e014eb4f54ae0ff740d2a4" :answer/id #uuid "ea6792e1-651e-5dba-ada4-cf70faf3410b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨-\\pi ,\\,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51321/selection/3c82cca794668e1e565df4e380928acad0b1afe1e5f4a6f72669b2546edbc814" :answer/id #uuid "e2603813-b585-5294-a4fe-573a8409febf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51321/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a428cf22-e48b-5d42-82ef-d2dd8fe48df8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-51321/selection/46959d84f4ab7edcbf6a72c5825078c3adf82b1a24e5ebe6f94127028ac0c909" :answer-field/choices ["q-51321/selection/0bf0647c0d1d4cbdf6d8778630c4c8d1a77f0c9076f89ec0ac34fbdb2aeb5145" "q-51321/selection/46959d84f4ab7edcbf6a72c5825078c3adf82b1a24e5ebe6f94127028ac0c909" "q-51321/selection/a1d6a6791698f26fa6ae881b564c930292d4d77c0a2dd67b51115a82631a6409" "q-51321/selection/2a23ad8446f30a46eec178d617017260911d066e90e014eb4f54ae0ff740d2a4" "q-51321/selection/3c82cca794668e1e565df4e380928acad0b1afe1e5f4a6f72669b2546edbc814"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-51321" :question/id #uuid "50417cb5-107a-5352-9dcc-5d6e3e271e0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-51321" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0-(\\frac{\\pi }{2})(1),1+(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-51321/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca363e2-c7b7-5196-bd38-10bcc30123ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51321"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352565/field-1/c338b0b4aaa881cbfd4adef738b15dd9be9d2bddcffd38cbdd76774da593d854" :answer/id #uuid "56141611-b3f3-585d-bc40-7ff5c9a2d06c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352565/field-1/d18a1bb9600f02e78f24b67126dbeff3638a4a289fa1abd25053ab6fa1636c52" :answer/id #uuid "771cc079-b1d6-5a20-a68c-3f45d46dfddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352565/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "13ec0303-a1ff-5b89-baa3-f527c12ce996" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352565/field-1/c338b0b4aaa881cbfd4adef738b15dd9be9d2bddcffd38cbdd76774da593d854" :answer-field/choices ["q-352565/field-1/c338b0b4aaa881cbfd4adef738b15dd9be9d2bddcffd38cbdd76774da593d854" "q-352565/field-1/d18a1bb9600f02e78f24b67126dbeff3638a4a289fa1abd25053ab6fa1636c52"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352565/field-2/f37b140e44c3c1469a0b674232c5aaeb4f71e6e7b8d79e0c213b062c66caacc7" :answer/id #uuid "4110d003-2c4e-5997-8900-fab7c7bdc9b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352565/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b79cc351-0f13-5b18-a69b-a1456fcb132a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352565/field-2/f37b140e44c3c1469a0b674232c5aaeb4f71e6e7b8d79e0c213b062c66caacc7" :answer-field/choices ["q-352565/field-2/f37b140e44c3c1469a0b674232c5aaeb4f71e6e7b8d79e0c213b062c66caacc7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352565" :question/id #uuid "06b8d700-c04c-547c-86d4-f00d7001a072" :question/math-academy-id "q-352565" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2\\pi t),\\,{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\pi t)⟩,\\,0<t<\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=\\frac{1}{8}.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$v(\\frac{1}{8})=⟨${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2\\pi t)),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({sin}^{2}⁡(2\\pi t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\pi {csc}^{2}⁡(2\\pi t),4\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=\\frac{1}{8},$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{1}{8}) & =⟨-4\\pi {csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),4\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\pi (\\sqrt{2})^{2},4\\pi (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\pi (2),4\\pi (\\frac{1}{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8\\pi ,\\,2\\pi ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352565/field-1" "q-352565/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca363e2-c7b7-5196-bd38-10bcc30123ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352565"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121724/selection/977e7f6eeac92045049ed829746d10945552245bfb0384cb0db71b2ea3a03613" :answer/id #uuid "554dd0fb-4208-5741-ae70-8224f5fb42b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(1)=⟨6,9\\operatorname{ln}⁡3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121724/selection/cdeafdcc99203dea056c58d6b7ec22070f5f0ceb26738cc7b82ae184da85366d" :answer/id #uuid "8778886f-7562-56c0-9a71-43e1e5347104" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(1)=⟨5,9⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121724/selection/6e9a3c6c46853ba62850b181ab53079895aaff5c30709d1ee36920d9910233ba" :answer/id #uuid "2689a1da-d0a5-52a7-8b9a-a669b0bfee8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(1)=⟨6,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121724/selection/6aaa2a6d37d4915ebe1985bcea771c6df87b328c3bff5c79f62f8fdbefe899c2" :answer/id #uuid "feb359a4-3b32-5e33-bc5e-49cb82f44588" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(1)=⟨6,3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121724/selection/f3d38ffa17d9a27bb89474e063e958177113177508baa7f4066e4b6aabe6b87c" :answer/id #uuid "1b7eb407-7b8e-58a6-acde-74af1e6c7ab5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(1)=⟨5,9\\operatorname{ln}⁡3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121724/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc9582a1-7444-5850-a75e-493e5c8599c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121724/selection/977e7f6eeac92045049ed829746d10945552245bfb0384cb0db71b2ea3a03613" :answer-field/choices ["q-121724/selection/977e7f6eeac92045049ed829746d10945552245bfb0384cb0db71b2ea3a03613" "q-121724/selection/cdeafdcc99203dea056c58d6b7ec22070f5f0ceb26738cc7b82ae184da85366d" "q-121724/selection/6e9a3c6c46853ba62850b181ab53079895aaff5c30709d1ee36920d9910233ba" "q-121724/selection/6aaa2a6d37d4915ebe1985bcea771c6df87b328c3bff5c79f62f8fdbefe899c2" "q-121724/selection/f3d38ffa17d9a27bb89474e063e958177113177508baa7f4066e4b6aabe6b87c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121724" :question/id #uuid "06760112-d5e2-54d2-a33b-b9a042a59cd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-121724" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨6t-1,{3}^{t+1}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t-1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({3}^{t+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,{3}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=1,$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨6,{3}^{1+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,{3}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,9\\operatorname{ln}⁡3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-121724/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca363e2-c7b7-5196-bd38-10bcc30123ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121724"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7152/selection/889adb1b863eac4340cded07ae58c6d5bf4dbf0e7d957a15591db82b627df9bf" :answer/id #uuid "d7851ad7-71c0-5da6-8fa7-adb674739c9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7152/selection/7bd73ccad642d682263fad81caa6942c9746cd1bcc61bee1c8617128c7d0d949" :answer/id #uuid "55c116de-6a6c-5511-9f39-ac07ab264e5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7152/selection/2e437e6d7421616a4cb11c4f5cb924a95509e04c02eac599dc42c90e7c269479" :answer/id #uuid "056d5332-bb24-5563-b911-7f4af2519835" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5e\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7152/selection/b9f70ecce203e7961ad36a121f8c87409e2321286ac5d4d2914120442ac46114" :answer/id #uuid "b613ef11-a6a5-5c17-b29e-1c93e0a17963" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7152/selection/8a273a1a3c81479d46be5f325e5c9101a864bb9b212d553de67a5b435a4f0e24" :answer/id #uuid "ecd74557-6af3-56fd-849d-46177f6b547e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7152/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "33bd199b-9413-5d91-8a13-367fba2bb3cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7152/selection/889adb1b863eac4340cded07ae58c6d5bf4dbf0e7d957a15591db82b627df9bf" :answer-field/choices ["q-7152/selection/889adb1b863eac4340cded07ae58c6d5bf4dbf0e7d957a15591db82b627df9bf" "q-7152/selection/7bd73ccad642d682263fad81caa6942c9746cd1bcc61bee1c8617128c7d0d949" "q-7152/selection/2e437e6d7421616a4cb11c4f5cb924a95509e04c02eac599dc42c90e7c269479" "q-7152/selection/b9f70ecce203e7961ad36a121f8c87409e2321286ac5d4d2914120442ac46114" "q-7152/selection/8a273a1a3c81479d46be5f325e5c9101a864bb9b212d553de67a5b435a4f0e24"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7152" :question/id #uuid "53b847c4-226d-5ecd-8eb4-77e4902d0d2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-7152" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2{t}^{2}+9⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=e.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}+9)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t,4t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=e,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(e) & =⟨2e\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+e,4e⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3e,4e⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=e$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(e),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(e)| & =\\sqrt{(3e)^{2}+(4e)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =5e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-7152/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "646467d1-f764-5a3c-b03b-7d74e588611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7152"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-7151"] :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2},\\,3t+7⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+7)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=4,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\nv=⟨4,3⟩\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=4$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(4),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(4)| & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed when $t=4$ is $5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-347189/field-1/1512fbc4ba9ac54935748bd30a3df0f8adcca19968544e9199178dd45a802f05" :answer/id #uuid "81eaeb4a-d2c5-5412-a7ad-56921d7c63f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347189/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "cca89a26-d9a9-538f-8154-57ee5207ee82" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347189/field-1/1512fbc4ba9ac54935748bd30a3df0f8adcca19968544e9199178dd45a802f05" :answer-field/choices ["q-347189/field-1/1512fbc4ba9ac54935748bd30a3df0f8adcca19968544e9199178dd45a802f05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347189" :question/id #uuid "2de309c1-86c0-5094-af8e-82af53f327aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-347189" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed $|v|$ of the particle at time $t=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe speed at time $t=3$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3}{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=3,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =⟨\\frac{1}{3+1},\\,-\\frac{3}{{3}^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=3$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(3),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(3)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{16}+\\frac{1}{9}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-347189/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "646467d1-f764-5a3c-b03b-7d74e588611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347189"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352587/field-1/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer/id #uuid "519e3928-5671-5cd0-9510-23e22caa7d2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352587/field-1/bc1aaa9670e8118cdb6ca0d3888d99928c842323e3d10885fe212d998358f89d" :answer/id #uuid "e2fb9704-94d7-5cda-8cda-568d7b42427c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352587/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "69ac440c-c275-5b9c-bb4e-c80f921cfff4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352587/field-1/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer-field/choices ["q-352587/field-1/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" "q-352587/field-1/bc1aaa9670e8118cdb6ca0d3888d99928c842323e3d10885fe212d998358f89d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352587" :question/id #uuid "67679c8a-32b4-5266-9ffd-bf77106d9a75" :question/math-academy-id "q-352587" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1),\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed $|v|$ of the particle at time $t=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe speed at time $t=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{2t+1},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=1,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨\\frac{2}{2(1)+1},\\,\\frac{1}{1+1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=1$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(1)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{9}+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352587/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "646467d1-f764-5a3c-b03b-7d74e588611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352587"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352583/field-1/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "26edb362-29ef-5dc8-8294-2df22990b811" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352583/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "42c5db93-17cd-5de7-86d6-737e596f3050" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352583/field-1/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer-field/choices ["q-352583/field-1/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352583" :question/id #uuid "7da9f9a5-a3d0-5aa7-9544-81bd3dbc19bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-352583" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\frac{{4}^{t-1}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4},\\frac{{9}^{t-1}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=1.$\n\nThe speed at time $t=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{4}^{t-1}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{9}^{t-1}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡9})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{4}^{t-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4},\\frac{{9}^{t-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{4}^{t-1},{9}^{t-1}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=1,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨{4}^{1-1},{9}^{1-1}⟩=⟨1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=1$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(1)| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352583/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "646467d1-f764-5a3c-b03b-7d74e588611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-51304"] :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{2}{e}^{-2t},\\,(t-1)^{3}⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}{e}^{-2t}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t{e}^{-2t}-2{t}^{2}{e}^{-2t},3(t-1)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t(1-t){e}^{-2t},3(t-1)^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨2t(1-t){e}^{-2t},3(t-1)^{2}⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2t(1-t){e}^{-2t}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=0,1, \\\\ 3(t-1)^{2}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=1$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-121738/selection/6cf833d30956b2ec4ddf97c8fde8ff95cb2caf00fc01abcf761505f046c22bb4" :answer/id #uuid "bb97c821-2f72-5c73-b2a4-59d22f624389" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121738/selection/24b44fba53578fd75922a19937c1240a9736e2dc7d7ad97ff6285932419cf4ea" :answer/id #uuid "5dec61cf-e12c-56dd-a6ff-fcf4c925b894" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121738/selection/7bb16478ce4217c08710f1c9f5ea7a1906fd0d8b3ecf4f594934d4e0d9644596" :answer/id #uuid "0b4651d6-be0b-552c-ac6e-e84b8c72b655" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121738/selection/95bc528a42f83cd4a53eb9e36d6b727f32c1b0eb864272fd8716dcc591ea8d15" :answer/id #uuid "4bc224e0-a347-5354-9f16-45c98cdccc96" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The particle is never stationary" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121738/selection/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" :answer/id #uuid "3f0ac3e1-44b9-5285-99f3-8808a297fb7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121738/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "05521e96-f8f3-5dfa-91c5-9d1469a7551a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121738/selection/24b44fba53578fd75922a19937c1240a9736e2dc7d7ad97ff6285932419cf4ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-121738/selection/6cf833d30956b2ec4ddf97c8fde8ff95cb2caf00fc01abcf761505f046c22bb4" "q-121738/selection/24b44fba53578fd75922a19937c1240a9736e2dc7d7ad97ff6285932419cf4ea" "q-121738/selection/7bb16478ce4217c08710f1c9f5ea7a1906fd0d8b3ecf4f594934d4e0d9644596" "q-121738/selection/95bc528a42f83cd4a53eb9e36d6b727f32c1b0eb864272fd8716dcc591ea8d15" "q-121738/selection/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121738" :question/id #uuid "1d55828e-407b-5591-939a-53be645784df" :question/math-academy-id "q-121738" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{3}-3t,{t}^{3}-6{t}^{2}+9t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-3t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-6{t}^{2}+9t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-3,3{t}^{2}-12t+9⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3({t}^{2}-1),3({t}^{2}-4t+3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3(t+1)(t-1),3(t-1)(t-3)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨3(t+1)(t-1),3(t-1)(t-3)⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(t+1)(t-1)=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=\\pm 1, \\\\ 3(t-1)(t-3)=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=1,3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=1$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121738/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11a24997-1f1e-5968-a331-980ca14be2f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121738"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347191/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "aa28a470-7f5e-57a0-8769-d5fca0aa9d8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347191/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1d01c8b-3216-5593-9bee-c9f9a05d357f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347191/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-347191/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347191" :question/id #uuid "ff983110-3b74-5a3a-aa83-a52d9b5e8cee" :question/math-academy-id "q-347191" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡((t-1)^{2}+2),(t-1)^{3}⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate the time at which the particle is stationary. Do not round the answer.\n\nThe particle is stationary at $t=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡((t-1)^{2}+2)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-1)^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2(t-1)}{(t-1)^{2}+2},\\,3(t-1)^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨\\frac{2(t-1)}{(t-1)^{2}+2},\\,3(t-1)^{2}⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(t-1)}{(t-1)^{2}+2}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=1, \\\\ 3(t-1)^{2}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=1$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-347191/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11a24997-1f1e-5968-a331-980ca14be2f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347191"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352722/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "8e787af9-72a7-5ef5-9fb2-fc1ccef61359" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352722/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "58ce2f09-6fa4-524b-b4d0-5d444e583556" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352722/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c62bea3-0021-5527-8d8b-aa124b36568c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352722/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-352722/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-352722/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352722" :question/id #uuid "300d663f-1d42-5d3b-99d8-47507ed9f5be" :question/math-academy-id "q-352722" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨(t-6)^{2}{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},\\,({t}^{2}-36)^{3}⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate the time at which the particle is stationary. Do not round the answer.\n\nThe particle is stationary at $t=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-6)^{2}{e}^{{t}^{2}-1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(({t}^{2}-36)^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2(t-6){e}^{{t}^{2}-1}+2t(t-6)^{2}{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},\\,6t({t}^{2}-36)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2(t-6)({t}^{2}-6t+1){e}^{{t}^{2}-1},\\,6t({t}^{2}-36)^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨2(t-6)({t}^{2}-6t+1){e}^{{t}^{2}-1},\\,6t({t}^{2}-36)^{2}⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(t-6)({t}^{2}-6t+1){e}^{{t}^{2}-1}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=6,\\text{ }3\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}, \\\\ 6t({t}^{2}-36)^{2}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=0,\\pm 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=6$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352722/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11a24997-1f1e-5968-a331-980ca14be2f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352722"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31654/selection/24b44fba53578fd75922a19937c1240a9736e2dc7d7ad97ff6285932419cf4ea" :answer/id #uuid "9dbae6bb-bb43-5bc0-b002-a4e5c364a4c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31654/selection/8b5a8474a9b9934bc051275be5cb046d57f79f1810a453d2a6924c7b768a1f5e" :answer/id #uuid "aae818a5-822e-555c-b2ef-1bed058b0416" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31654/selection/7161f3140020b0dd4c15ea58a14042b8788c2ceccaa922c051ca801a7112dea6" :answer/id #uuid "207bcb60-0693-51c7-aba8-96defca8dfd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31654/selection/95bc528a42f83cd4a53eb9e36d6b727f32c1b0eb864272fd8716dcc591ea8d15" :answer/id #uuid "01976a4f-3098-54eb-b904-2732ba756ec0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The particle is never stationary" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31654/selection/bddb16fb60275d07c2d2a20d0ff2251caf856d27ab8e69dbd10410685c39553a" :answer/id #uuid "fdd7ee11-39e5-5903-9623-bfb0b41baf09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31654/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "333d07b7-e297-52fc-8269-a583519011b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-31654/selection/95bc528a42f83cd4a53eb9e36d6b727f32c1b0eb864272fd8716dcc591ea8d15" :answer-field/choices ["q-31654/selection/24b44fba53578fd75922a19937c1240a9736e2dc7d7ad97ff6285932419cf4ea" "q-31654/selection/8b5a8474a9b9934bc051275be5cb046d57f79f1810a453d2a6924c7b768a1f5e" "q-31654/selection/7161f3140020b0dd4c15ea58a14042b8788c2ceccaa922c051ca801a7112dea6" "q-31654/selection/95bc528a42f83cd4a53eb9e36d6b727f32c1b0eb864272fd8716dcc591ea8d15" "q-31654/selection/bddb16fb60275d07c2d2a20d0ff2251caf856d27ab8e69dbd10410685c39553a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-31654" :question/id #uuid "40f57e73-e666-5019-bdd1-73bff2dc4f02" :question/math-academy-id "q-31654" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{3}-3t,\\,2{t}^{2}+6t-3⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-3t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}+6t-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-3,4t+6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3({t}^{2}-1),2(2t+3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3(t-1)(t+1),2(2t+3)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨3(t-1)(t+1),2(2t+3)⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(t-1)(t+1)=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=\\pm 1, \\\\ 2(2t+3)=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is no value of $t$ that satisfies both equations, so there are no stationary points." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-31654/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11a24997-1f1e-5968-a331-980ca14be2f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31654"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-616"] :question/problem "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t > 0$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 3t^3, 2t^2\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}.$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-617"] :question/problem "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t > 0$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 12t, 2t^3\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}$ at time $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12,6{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=1$, we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨12,6(1)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-618"] :question/problem "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t > 0$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 6t^2+2, 2t^3\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}+2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12t,6{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2$, we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨12(2),6(2)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨24,24⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=2$ we calculate the magnitude of $\\mathbf{v}(2),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(2)| & =\\sqrt{{24}^{2}+{24}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2({24}^{2})} \\\\  & =24\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed when $t=2$ is $24\\sqrt{2}\\approx 33.94$ to two decimal places." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-619"] :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle t^2-2t, t^3-3t \\rangle, \\quad t\\in[0,\\infty).\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-3t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨2t-2,3{t}^{2}-3⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2t-2 & =0\\,⇒\\,t=1, \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-3 & =0\\,⇒\\,t=\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $t=-1$ is outside of the domain of $t,$ so we discard it. \n\nThe solution $t=1$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only time when the object is stationary." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
